(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The regular-expression engine of the module _sre (PY6a; Modules/_sre/sre_lib.h's SRE(match), its semantics"] [4 1 "// over the code re._compiler emits): a backtracking matcher, iterative as sre_lib.h's (queue 202): its"] [5 1 "// backtracking points (a branch's next alternative, a single-item repeat's next count, a repeat's other choice"] [6 1 "// at its UNTIL) on an explicit stack, and the bodies that end in SUCCESS (asserts, atomic groups, possessive"] [7 1 "// repeats' iterations) on a stack of frames, so a repetition's length costs heap, not Go's stack. The marks"] [8 1 "// (groups' bounds), lastindex and lastmark are saved at each backtracking point and restored when it is taken."] [9 1 "// Characters are code points (str) or byte values (bytes)."] [11 1 "// The opcodes, in re._constants.OPCODES' order (its values are the indexes)."] [58 1 "// AT codes and categories, in re._constants' orders."] [95 32 "// _sre.MAXREPEAT (SRE_MAXREPEAT for a 4-byte code)"] [97 1 "// sreState is one match attempt's state (SRE_STATE)."] [101 18 "// the search's bounds (pos, endpos)"] [109 25 "// the backtracking points"] [110 25 "// the bodies entered"] [111 25 "// until's answer"] [114 1 "// sreRep is a REPEAT's context for one iteration (SRE_REPEAT): the count of completed iterations, the"] [115 1 "// position the last iteration began at (the zero-width guard), the enclosing context. Never written once made, so"] [116 1 "// a backtracking point keeps it as it was."] [135 1 "// sreIsWordUni is SRE_UNI_IS_WORD: Py_UNICODE_ISALNUM or '_', by CPython's Unicode database."] [140 1 "// sreLowerUni and sreUpperUni are sre_lower_unicode and sre_upper_unicode: the simple case mappings of CPython's"] [141 1 "// Unicode database (_PyUnicode_ToLowercase, _PyUnicode_ToUppercase), which re._compiler's case tables come from too."] [145 1 "// sreUpperLocale is sre_upper_locale in the C locale: ASCII's (sre_lower_locale is sreLowerASCII)."] [153 1 "// sreCharLocIgnore is char_loc_ignore: the pattern's literal p (not lower-cased under LOCALE) and c, c's lower or"] [154 1 "// its upper case."] [201 1 "// sreCharsetMatch is SRE(charset): the set at pc (up to its FAILURE) contains c."] [220 4 "// 256 bits in 8 words of 32"] [234 24 "// c is lower-cased already"] [243 4 "// count, then 256 block indices (64 words of 4 bytes, little-endian), then count blocks of 8 words"] [262 1 "// charsetLocIgnore is SRE(charset_loc_ignore): both locale cases of c against every member of the set at pc, so the"] [263 1 "// set is closed under case before it is complemented ([^bc] does not match b'B')."] [305 1 "// single is one width-one item at pc matching s[pos] (SRE(count)'s cases), and the item's length."] [381 1 "// The backtracking points' kinds: what a DO_JUMP of sre_lib.h's SRE(match) does when its jump fails."] [383 27 "// BRANCH: pc the alternative tried last (its skip word), the next one tried"] [384 27 "// REPEAT_ONE: pc the op, n the count tried last, one fewer next (down to min)"] [385 27 "// MIN_REPEAT_ONE: pc the op, n the count tried last, one more next (up to max)"] [386 27 "// MAX_UNTIL's iteration failed: the tail at pc, pos, with rep"] [387 27 "// MIN_UNTIL's tail failed: another iteration at pc, pos, with rep (nil: none)"] [388 27 "// the sentinel of the innermost frame: its body failed"] [391 1 "// sreBt is a backtracking point with sre_lib.h's saved state: LASTMARK_SAVE's lastmark and lastindex, restored when"] [392 1 "// the point is taken (restore), and MARK_PUSH's marks[0..lastmark] (pushed: sre pushes them only inside a repeat,"] [393 1 "// state->repeat, for most ops). A point's saved marks are never written, so a point kept for its next choice keeps"] [394 1 "// them."] [405 1 "// The frames' kinds: a body ended by SUCCESS (sre's DO_JUMP0, not toplevel) that does not backtrack into the code"] [406 1 "// after it: asserts, atomic groups, possessive repeats' iterations (those up to min, then the others)."] [415 1 "// sreFrame is a body being matched: its op's pc, the position it was entered at (a possessive repeat's: its"] [416 1 "// iteration's), the repeat context to go on with after it, the iterations a possessive repeat completed before"] [417 1 "// this one, and its sentinel's index in the backtracking stack. When the body reaches SUCCESS the backtracking"] [418 1 "// points above the sentinel are dropped."] [427 1 "// push is a backtracking point: LASTMARK_SAVE, and MARK_PUSH when pushed."] [437 1 "// restore is MARK_POP (or MARK_POP_KEEP) and LASTMARK_RESTORE of a point that saved them."] [448 1 "// enter starts a frame's body; its sentinel restores as the op's failure does."] [454 1 "// leave drops the innermost frame with its sentinel and every backtracking point above it (MARK_POP_DISCARD)."] [465 1 "// pop drops the newest backtracking point."] [471 1 "// possessive goes on after a possessive repeat's iteration at pc (the op) completed count iterations at pos, the last"] [472 1 "// one begun at last (-1 when none was begun past min; POSSESSIVE_REPEAT's loops): the next iteration's body's pc, or"] [473 1 "// the tail's (past the body's SUCCESS) with st.rep the repeat context outside."] [477 40 "// sre's state->repeat, non-NULL in the body"] [491 1 "// match runs the code from pc at pos: SRE(match) of sre_lib.h, iterative as it is, its DO_JUMPs' contexts an explicit"] [492 1 "// stack of backtracking points (st.bt) and its DO_JUMP0s' bodies a stack of frames (st.frames), so no repetition grows"] [493 1 "// Go's stack; the marks saved and restored where sre's are (LASTMARK_SAVE, MARK_PUSH), so a group's span after"] [494 1 "// backtracking is CPython's. A SUCCESS outside every frame is the match's end, if accept takes it."] [522 17 "// MARK_POP_DISCARD: the marks the body set stay"] [565 5 "// a minimum width the rest needs"] [578 6 "// the marks between the last valid one and this one were not reached"] [629 5 "// a tail beginning with a literal is tried only where the literal is (sre's optimization)"] [708 3 "// backtrack: the newest point's next choice, its saved state restored first"] [762 6 "// the iteration failed: the tail, at the position it began at"] [771 1 "// branch is the first alternative from i (a skip word) that its first op does not rule out at pos (sre's BRANCH skips"] [772 1 "// an alternative whose LITERAL or IN does not match), -1 when none is left."] [791 1 "// until is MAX_UNTIL or MIN_UNTIL for the repeat context r, an iteration just completed at pos (sre_lib.h's cases):"] [792 1 "// the pc to go on at, the repeat context to go on with in st.rep, the other choice pushed as a backtracking point."] [816 2 "// MIN_UNTIL: the tail first; the marks pushed only if the tail is inside a repeat (sre's repeat_of_tail)"] [826 1 "// run tries a match at pos (SRE(match)): true with the marks set, and the match's end."] [844 1 "// search is SRE(search): the first position from st.start at which run succeeds."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[458 21] [458 37] [579 30] [579 37] [680 15] [680 22] [775 6] [775 20] [846 21] [846 36] [847 28]]} (go/file "sre.go" :imports [])

;; The regular-expression engine of the module _sre (PY6a; Modules/_sre/sre_lib.h's SRE(match), its semantics
;; over the code re._compiler emits): a backtracking matcher, iterative as sre_lib.h's (queue 202): its
;; backtracking points (a branch's next alternative, a single-item repeat's next count, a repeat's other choice
;; at its UNTIL) on an explicit stack, and the bodies that end in SUCCESS (asserts, atomic groups, possessive
;; repeats' iterations) on a stack of frames, so a repetition's length costs heap, not Go's stack. The marks
;; (groups' bounds), lastindex and lastmark are saved at each backtracking point and restored when it is taken.
;; Characters are code points (str) or byte values (bytes).


